      <encodingDesc>
         <appInfo>
            <application>
               <name>musiconn.scoresearch</name>
               <p>Source OMR data.</p>
            </application>
            <application isodate="YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss" version="VERSION">
               <name>Verovio</name>
               <p>Transcoded source data from MusicXML to MEI.</p>
            </application>
            <application startdate="YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss" enddate="YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss" version="VERSION">
               <name>mei-friend</name>
               <p>Manual correction and editorial review.</p>
            </application>
         </appInfo>
         <editorialDecl>
            <p>This is a corrected digital edition based on DdT 1903. OMR and conversion errors are corrected against its facsimile. Substantive departures from DdT are documented in editorial annotations recording the source reading, encoded reading, evidence or conjectural reasoning, and responsible editor. Historical prints consulted for comparison are identified in sourceDesc; source-supported and conjectural emendations are distinguished.</p>
            <!-- Tailor this paragraph to the actual work and staff arrangement. -->
            <p>The keyboard realization printed in DdT is retained as part of that edition. It is distinguished from the figured continuo bass transmitted in the historical print and must be selected explicitly when defining an analytical view.</p>
            <p>Original page and system boundaries are represented by pb and sb elements. Surface and page-break numbers form a work-local sequence beginning with 1; the printed page range is recorded in sourceDesc. Each measure points to a measure zone on the corresponding facsimile surface using @facs.</p>
         </editorialDecl>
         <projectDesc>
            <p>This edition was prepared by CAMAT Corpus Editions as part of a DFG-funded corpus for music-analysis technologies (grant PF 669/18-1).</p>
         </projectDesc>
